---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Badge } from '@highjack/ui';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Game — HighJack"
  description="How a HighJack match is composed: the application surface, the rendered table, and the authoritative deterministic simulation underneath."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="m-0 font-display text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">The game</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 mb-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      A HighJack match is one thing at every level: a configurable ruleset, executed by an
      authoritative simulation. Here's how that becomes something you can see and touch.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Anatomy -->
  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="anatomy-title">
    <h2 id="anatomy-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">
      Anatomy of the client
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-500">
          Application layer
        </p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-2 font-display text-xl font-bold">Menus · panels · negotiation</h3>
        <p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Lobbies, trade desks, auction rooms, casino tables, event tickers, and settings live in a
          crisp SolidJS interface. Fast, accessible, keyboard-friendly — everything you read and
          click.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-500">Render layer</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-2 font-display text-xl font-bold">The board, alive</h3>
        <p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          The board itself is a GPU-rendered PixiJS stage: tactile pieces, dealt cards, chip
          physics, event effects. The two layers stay cleanly separated — UI never fights pixels.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Authority diagram -->
  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="authority-title">
    <h2 id="authority-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">
      Who decides what happens
    </h2>
    <div
      class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-felt-900/50 p-6 shadow-card"
      tabindex={0}
      aria-label="Action flow diagram, scrollable"
    >
      <pre
        class="m-0 min-w-[28rem] font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-400 sm:text-sm"><code>Your move
   ↓
Action (validated against current state)
   ↓
Authoritative engine — one deterministic transition
   ↓
Events (what changed)
   ↓
New state → everyone sees the same truth</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      Clients never decide outcomes; they propose actions. The server's engine validates and applies
      each one atomically, then broadcasts the events. Deterministic seeds mean any match can be
      replayed move-for-move — great for debugging, better for trust.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Honest status + shell pointer -->
  <section
    class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-gold-700/40 bg-gold-700/10 p-6"
    aria-label="Development status"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">
      Current status
      <Badge tone="gold">Shell only</Badge>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cream-300">
      What exists today: this website, the game-client shell (application chrome over a live render
      stage), the engine skeleton with real lifecycle rules, the wire protocol, and the Go backend.
      Board gameplay begins with the next milestone. Run the shell locally with:
      <code class="ml-1 rounded bg-felt-950 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-gold-400"
        >bun run dev:game</code
      >
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Roadmap teaser -->
  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="roadmap-title">
    <h2 id="roadmap-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">The road ahead</h2>
    <ol class="mt-6 list-none space-y-3 p-0">
      <li class="flex items-start gap-4 rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-4">
        <span
          class="hj-numerals shrink-0 rounded-md bg-teal-600/20 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-teal-400"
          >v0.1</span
        >
        <span class="text-sm text-muted-400"
          ><strong class="text-cream-100">Foundation</strong> — architecture, protocol, design system,
          website, backend. Shipped.</span
        >
      </li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-4 rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-4">
        <span
          class="hj-numerals shrink-0 rounded-md bg-gold-700/25 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-gold-400"
          >v0.2</span
        >
        <span class="text-sm text-muted-400"
          ><strong class="text-cream-100">First table</strong> — core board loop: movement, property,
          rent, bankruptcy.</span
        >
      </li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-4 rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-4">
        <span
          class="hj-numerals shrink-0 rounded-md bg-felt-700 px-2 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-muted-400"
          >v0.3+</span
        >
        <span class="text-sm text-muted-400"
          ><strong class="text-cream-100">The chaos catalog</strong> — trading, auctions, gambling tables,
          carnival, sports, global events.</span
        >
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
